sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Monitor
  actor Admin as SYSTEM_ADMIN
  participant FE as Vue UI
  participant API as GAS Router / Controller
  participant Settings as AdministrationOperations
  participant DB as Sheets
  Monitor->>API: GET system.health (public)
  API-->>Monitor: Minimal bootstrap status, no secrets
  Admin->>FE: View or edit settings
  FE->>API: system.config.get(sessionToken)
  API->>API: Require system.settings.read
  API->>DB: Read two vc_settings keys
  API-->>FE: Bounded setting values
  FE->>API: system.config.update(values)
  API->>API: Require system.settings.manage
  alt Valid keys and integer bounds
    API->>Settings: updateSettings()
    Settings->>DB: Update vc_settings and append audit
    API-->>FE: Updated setting values
  else Invalid / unauthorized
    API-->>FE: INVALID_SETTINGS / FORBIDDEN
  end
  Admin->>FE: Reset data for test / set-up (VC-ADR-039)
  FE->>API: system.reset.preview(keepUsers, keepCampaigns)
  API->>API: Require system.reset and host switch
  API->>DB: Read all tables, count rows to delete, plan digest
  API-->>FE: Counts deleted / kept, Drive file count, phrase
  FE->>API: system.reset.execute(phrase, password, planDigest)
  alt Phrase, password and unchanged plan
    API->>DB: Delete non-master rows (batches)
    API->>Drive: trashAll photo folder (Drive trash)
    API->>DB: Append SYSTEM_RESET audit
    API-->>FE: Deleted counts and Drive status
  else Wrong phrase / password / stale plan / switched off
    API-->>FE: RESET_CONFIRMATION_INVALID / INVALID_CREDENTIALS / RESET_PLAN_STALE / OPERATION_DISABLED
  end
  Admin->>FE: Set which logs are kept and for how long (VC-ADR-040)
  FE->>API: system.config.update({log_policy: [{code, enabled, days} x5]})
  alt Every kind, days in range, required logs on
    API->>DB: Save vc_settings log_policy + LOG_POLICY_UPDATED audit
    API-->>FE: Settings + log_policy + log_counts
  else Invalid / required log switched off
    API-->>FE: INVALID_LOG_POLICY / LOG_REQUIRED
  end
  Note over API,DB: Every later log write: switched-off kind not written; kept row gets expire_at (Firestore TTL)
